## 5. Key Analytical Findings

### Customer Acquisition
- 1,000 registered customers.
- Monthly customer acquisition was analyzed to identify registration trends.

### Trial-to-Paid Conversion

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Trial subscription lifecycles | 1,150 |
| Converted lifecycles | 1,091 |
| Conversion rate | 94.87% |

### Subscription Churn

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Total subscription lifecycles | 1,150 |
| Ended subscriptions | 361 |
| Lifecycle churn rate | 31.39% |

### Active Subscription Distribution

A total of **791 subscription lifecycles** were active on December 31, 2025.

### Plan Transitions

- 95 monthly-to-annual billing transitions.
- 84 plan downgrade events.
- Average interval between the preceding event and a monthly-to-annual transition: 188.76 days.

### Customer Lifecycle & Retention

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Customers with multiple lifecycles | 150 |
| Percentage of customers with multiple lifecycles | 15.00% |
| Eligible lifecycles for 90-day retention | 950 |
| Retained after 90 days | 858 |
| 90-day lifecycle retention rate | 90.32% |

### Revenue Analytics

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Total payment records | 6,191 |
| Subscription lifecycles with payments | 1,091 |
| Total simulated revenue | $180,144.09 |
| Average payment | $29.10 |

#### Revenue by Plan

| Plan | Frequency | Revenue (USD) |
|---|---|---:|
| Family | Annual | 49,317.26 |
| Premium | Annual | 35,637.03 |
| Family | Monthly | 34,202.89 |
| Premium | Monthly | 23,693.76 |
| Basic | Annual | 20,607.71 |
| Basic | Monthly | 16,685.44 |

### Business Insights

- Family Annual generated the highest revenue among the six paid plan configurations.
- Basic Monthly generated the highest number of payment records but the lowest total revenue.
- Annual billing contributed approximately 58.6% of total simulated revenue.
- 15% of customers had more than one subscription lifecycle, indicating repeat subscription activity in the simulated dataset.

## 6. Technical Skills

- Microsoft SQL Server and T-SQL
- Data profiling and validation
- Joins and aggregations
- Common Table Expressions (CTEs)
- CASE expressions
- Window functions: ROW_NUMBER() and LAG()
- Date calculations
- Customer lifecycle and retention analysis
- Recursive payment scheduling
- Revenue analysis

## 7. Assumptions & Limitations

- All source data is synthetic.
- Revenue represents simulated subscription payments, not verified cash collected.
- No prorated charges or refunds are modeled.
- Annual billing changes trigger an immediate payment and reset the billing cycle.
- Plan changes apply to the next scheduled payment.
- The immediate post-trial cancellation metric could not be reliably calculated because the event records did not contain subscriptions with both TRIAL_EXPIRED and CANCELLED events.
- Conversion, churn, and retention rates are calculated at the subscription-lifecycle level unless otherwise specified.
- The 188.76-day upgrade measure represents the interval between the preceding event and the billing transition, not necessarily the exact time spent on monthly billing.

